# Line-ending policy.
#
# Default: normalise every text file to LF in the repository.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The Windows launchers MUST be checked out with CRLF.
#
# This is not cosmetic. wscript reads .vbs as ANSI/GBK on Chinese Windows; a
# mangled GBK double-byte sequence can swallow a bare LF, merging two lines and
# producing a bogus "800A0400 / 缺少语句" compile error with a wrong line number.
# cmd.exe batch files have their own LF quirks around labels and multi-line
# constructs. Neither failure is obvious from the source text.
#
# See AGENTS.md §1 and docs/TROUBLESHOOTING.md §3.
*.vbs   text eol=crlf
*.bat   text eol=crlf
*.cmd   text eol=crlf
*.ps1   text eol=crlf

# Runtime artefacts are never text.
*.log   binary
